# The corpus is hashed BYTE-EXACTLY by Corpus::digest(), and the digest
# deliberately does not normalise line endings — a mangled checkout really is
# different content and should say so.
#
# That only works if the bytes are the same everywhere to begin with. With mixed
# endings in the tree, a consumer whose git has core.autocrlf=true computes a
# different digest from a Linux CI runner FOR IDENTICAL CONTENT, and the
# cross-check reads that as a stale artifact when nothing is stale.
#
# A drift detector that fires on non-drift trains people to ignore it, and then
# it is worth nothing when it fires correctly. So: LF, pinned, everywhere.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.json   text eol=lf
*.md     text eol=lf
*.php    text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
*.js     text eol=lf
*.mjs    text eol=lf
*.ts     text eol=lf
*.yml    text eol=lf
*.toml   text eol=lf
VERSION  text eol=lf
py.typed text eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
